{% comment %}
  Walterin · Buy section (product page). Used by product templates; main-product is untouched.
  Design system: assets/walterin-ui.css (body.wui). Behaviour: assets/walterin-buy.js.
  Rules: docs/design/BUY-SECTION-SPEC.md.

  Direction "Frameless": type and space carry the column. The only framed things are the
  email field and the one yellow button; everything else is text, a dot, a marker and a rule.

  Order (one vertical rhythm, groups 40 desktop / 32 mobile apart):
    1. Title            product title, one headline
    2. Price            price + shipping line with its icon
    3. Choice           one group per product option (Language, Format, …)
    4. Act              add to cart (+ express checkout + payment icons) or notify me
    5. Read             accordions: About, What's in the box (+ product safety), Delivery, extras

  Options are generic: one group per product option, so the same section serves the tarot
  (Language) and the books (Format × Language). "Option value" blocks give a value its short
  code; the name shown always comes from the site language (locales walterin.buy.value.*),
  so an English site never shows a Slovak word and the other way round.

  States (snippets/product-state.liquid): coming_soon → notify form · available → add to cart
  · sold_out → faded, disabled button. Unavailable combinations stay visible, faded, unclickable.

  Every visible word is a setting or a locale string, so Translate & Adapt can translate it.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  # Everything this page says about THIS product comes from one place: the walterin metafields.
  # The section's own settings hold only what is identical on every product — button labels,
  # screen-reader text, the payment blocklist. See docs/CONTENT-MODEL.md.
  assign wui = product.metafields.walterin

  assign preview = 'real'
  # The preview states are for review only: the theme editor, and preview/development themes.
  # On the published theme (theme.role == 'main') visitors always see the real product state.
  if request.design_mode or theme.role != 'main'
    assign preview = section.settings.editor_state
  endif

  capture product_state
    render 'product-state', product: product
  endcapture
  assign product_state = product_state | strip
  if preview == 'buyable' or preview == 'first_sold_out' or preview == 'low_stock'
    assign product_state = 'available'
  elsif preview == 'sold_out'
    assign product_state = 'sold_out'
  endif

  assign selected = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  if preview == 'first_sold_out' and product.variants.size > 1
    assign selected = product.variants[1]
  endif
  assign selected_available = selected.available
  if preview == 'buyable' or preview == 'first_sold_out' or preview == 'low_stock'
    assign selected_available = true
  endif
  assign price = selected.price | money_without_trailing_zeros

  comment
    ---- Launch gate ----

    A date belongs to a variant, not a product: Walterin Prague's eBook opens on
    23 October and its printed edition on 10 November, so between those two
    dates one edition sells and the other does not. Every date comes from
    snippets/launch-date.liquid.

    Before its date a variant is never "sold out" — it has not been for sale
    yet. It shows the date and the notify form instead, and the buy button is
    not there at all. On the morning of its launch day the comparison below
    flips by itself and the button appears. Nothing has to be remembered.

    The eBook is untracked on purpose, so after its date Shopify never blocks it
    and it can never read "Sold out". The printed book and the tarot are tracked,
    so once they launch their stock decides, exactly as it should.

    today is taken in the store's own timezone, so the switch happens at local
    midnight rather than UTC.
  endcomment
  assign today = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0

  capture selected_launch
    render 'launch-date', product: product, variant: selected
  endcapture
  assign selected_launch = selected_launch | strip
  assign selected_launched = true
  if selected_launch == 'soon'
    assign selected_launched = false
  elsif selected_launch != blank
    assign selected_launch_n = selected_launch | plus: 0
    if selected_launch_n > today
      assign selected_launched = false
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Which CTAs need to exist in the markup at all. Both can be present at once —
    a visitor switching from the printed edition to the eBook moves between them
    without a page load, so JavaScript hides and shows, it never invents markup.
  endcomment
  assign any_buyable = false
  assign any_waiting = false
  for v in product.variants
    capture v_launch
      render 'launch-date', product: product, variant: v
    endcapture
    assign v_launch = v_launch | strip
    assign v_launched = true
    if v_launch == 'soon'
      assign v_launched = false
    elsif v_launch != blank
      assign v_launch_n = v_launch | plus: 0
      if v_launch_n > today
        assign v_launched = false
      endif
    endif
    if v_launched and v.available
      assign any_buyable = true
    else
      assign any_waiting = true
    endif
  endfor

  if preview == 'buyable' or preview == 'first_sold_out' or preview == 'low_stock'
    assign any_buyable = true
    assign selected_launched = true
  endif

  comment
    An unlaunched selection is a coming-soon page, whatever the stock says.
  endcomment
  if selected_launched == false and product_state != 'sold_out'
    assign product_state = 'coming_soon'
  endif
  if selected_launched == false
    assign selected_available = false
  endif

  comment
    The line above the email field: "Available from October 23rd". It is built
    from the date itself, so it cannot drift out of step with the gate, and it
    disappears on launch day with the rest.
  endcomment
  assign selected_launch_label = ''
  if selected_launch == 'soon'
    assign selected_launch_label = 'walterin.launch.soon' | t
  elsif selected_launch != blank
    assign date_key = 'walterin.launch.date_' | append: selected_launch
    assign date_name = date_key | t
    assign selected_launch_label = 'walterin.launch.from' | t | replace: '[date]', date_name
  endif

  assign form_id = 'WuiBuyForm-' | append: section.id
  assign notify_id = 'WuiNotify-' | append: section.id
  assign buy_id = 'WuiBuy-' | append: section.id

  assign digital = true
  if selected.requires_shipping
    assign digital = false
  endif

-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The waitlist tag. The product's own handle names the list; the chosen variant's SKU names the
  edition. It has to be the SKU: an option value is translated, so on /sk/ "English" becomes
  "Angličtina" and the same campaign would split into two tags. A SKU never changes language.

  No SKU set yet? Fall back to the variant's position so the tag is still stable, and say so in the
  theme editor — the same way gpsr-row warns about missing safety information.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign waitlist_tag = product.handle | append: '-waitlist'
  assign selected_code = ''
  assign missing_sku = false
  unless product.has_only_default_variant
    if selected.sku != blank
      assign selected_code = selected.sku | handleize
    else
      assign missing_sku = true
      for v in product.variants
        if v.id == selected.id
          assign selected_code = 'v' | append: forloop.index
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endunless
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The name of the chosen edition, used in the notify message and the sticky bar. A single-variant
  product has no edition — Shopify calls it "Default Title" — so it stays empty and the [edition]
  placeholder drops out of the sentence instead of naming a thing that does not exist.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture selected_name_html -%}
  {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}<span data-wui-edname>{{ selected.option1 | escape }}</span>{%- endunless -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture price_html -%}<span data-wui-price>{{ price }}</span>{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if product_state == 'available' -%}
  <script src="{{ 'product-form.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
<script src="{{ 'walterin-buy.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

<div
  class="wui-scope wui-buy"
  id="{{ buy_id }}"
  data-wui-buy
  data-state="{{ product_state }}"
  data-pswp-core="{{ 'photoswipe.esm.min.js' | asset_url }}"
  data-pswp-lightbox="{{ 'photoswipe-lightbox.esm.min.js' | asset_url }}"
  data-pswp-css="{{ 'photoswipe.css' | asset_url }}"
  data-sold-out="{{ 'walterin.buy.sold_out' | t | escape }}"
  data-unavailable="{{ 'walterin.buy.unavailable' | t | escape }}"
  data-switched="{{ 'walterin.buy.switched' | t | escape }}"
>
  <div class="wui-wrap wui-buy__grid">
    {%- comment -%} ================= Gallery ================= {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="wui-buy__gallery">
      <div class="wui-frame wui-gallery__main">
        <div
          class="wui-gallery__track"
          data-wui-track
          tabindex="0"
          aria-label="{{ section.settings.gallery_label | escape }}"
        >
          {%- for media in product.media -%}
            {%- if media.media_type == 'image' -%}
              <div class="wui-gallery__slide" id="WuiSlide-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }}" data-wui-slide>
                <a
                  class="wui-gallery__zoom"
                  href="{{ media | image_url: width: 2400 }}"
                  data-wui-zoom
                  data-pswp-width="{{ media.width }}"
                  data-pswp-height="{{ media.height }}"
                  aria-label="{{ section.settings.zoom_label | escape }}{% if media.alt != blank %}: {{ media.alt | escape }}{% endif %}"
                >
                  {{
                    media
                    | image_url: width: 1600
                    | image_tag:
                      widths: '400, 600, 800, 1000, 1300, 1600',
                      sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 46vw, 92vw',
                      alt: media.alt,
                      loading: 'eager'
                  }}
                </a>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
        {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
          <span class="wui-gallery__count" aria-hidden="true" data-wui-count>1 / {{ product.media.size }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
        <nav class="wui-gallery__thumbs" aria-label="{{ section.settings.thumbs_label | escape }}">
          {%- for media in product.media -%}
            {%- if media.media_type == 'image' -%}
              <a
                class="wui-gallery__thumb"
                href="#WuiSlide-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }}"
                data-wui-thumb
                aria-current="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                aria-label="{{ section.settings.thumbs_label | escape }} {{ forloop.index }}"
              >
                {{- media | image_url: width: 200 | image_tag: alt: '', loading: 'lazy', sizes: '80px', widths: '100, 200' -}}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </nav>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ================= Buy column ================= {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="wui-buy__box">
      {%- comment -%} ---- 1 + 2. Title and price ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="wui-buy__head">
        <h1 class="wui-heading wui-buy__title">{{ product.title | escape | replace: ': ', ':<br>' }}</h1>
        <div class="wui-buy__price">
          <p class="wui-buy__amount">{{ price_html }}</p>
          {%- comment -%}
            Tax wording only when Shopify's "Include tax in prices" is on (cart.taxes_included).
            Walterin is not a VAT payer: that setting stays off → no VAT wording, no theme change later.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Availability sits in the price row (Veronka, 6 Oct 2026): the answer
            to "can I have this" belongs next to the price, not further down the
            page, and it takes the shipping line's place rather than crowding it.

            The row is always in the markup and hidden when there is nothing to
            say, because the script fills it as the visitor changes edition — if
            it were only printed when the first edition happened to have a label,
            an edition chosen later would silently show nothing.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p
            class="wui-buy__pill-row"
            data-wui-launch-line
            {% if selected_launch_label == blank %}hidden{% endif %}
          >
            <span class="wui-pill" data-wui-launch-pill>{{ selected_launch_label }}</span>
          </p>
          <p class="wui-buy__ship wui-iconline" data-wui-ship {% if digital %}hidden{% endif %}>
            {%- render 'wui-icon', icon: 'shipping' -%}
            <span>
              {%- if cart.taxes_included -%}{{ 'products.product.include_taxes' | t }} {% endif -%}
              {{- 'walterin.buy.shipping' | t -}}
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        ---- 3. Choice: one group per product option ----
        A product with a single variant has no real options: Shopify still reports one called
        "Title" holding "Default Title". Rendering that would put a legend and a pill on the page
        for a choice nobody has. `has_only_default_variant` is the guard.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- capture option_groups -%}
        <div class="wui-buy__choices">
        {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
        {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign opt_index = forloop.index
            assign values_count = option.values.size
            assign longest = 0
            for value in option.values
              assign words = value | split: ' '
              for w in words
                assign wl = w | size
                if wl > longest
                  assign longest = wl
                endif
              endfor
            endfor
          -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign opt_slug = option.name | handleize
            assign opt_key = 'walterin.buy.option.' | append: opt_slug
            assign opt_name = opt_key | t
            assign opt_check = opt_name | downcase
            if opt_check contains 'translation missing'
              assign opt_name = option.name
            endif
          -%}
          <div class="wui-cq wui-buy__option">
            <fieldset class="wui-buy__fieldset">
              <legend class="wui-label wui-buy__legend">{{ opt_name | escape }}</legend>
              <div
                class="wui-choices{% if longest >= 11 %} wui-choices--long{% endif %}"
                data-n="{{ values_count }}"
                data-option="{{ opt_index }}"
                style="--wui-n: {{ values_count }};"
              >
                {%- for value in option.values -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign key = value | downcase | strip
                    assign v_code = value | handleize
                    for pair in pairs
                      assign parts = pair | strip | split: '|'
                      if parts[0] == key and parts[1] != blank
                        assign v_code = parts[1]
                      endif
                    endfor

                    assign name_key = 'walterin.buy.value.' | append: v_code
                    assign v_name = name_key | t
                    assign v_name_check = v_name | downcase
                    if v_name_check contains 'translation missing'
                      assign v_name = value
                    endif

                    # Availability of this value, rendered server-side so the first paint is already
                    # right: walterin-buy.js recalculates the same text and nothing moves.
                    assign v_any_available = false
                    assign v_left = 0
                    for variant in product.variants
                      assign v_match = false
                      if opt_index == 1 and variant.option1 == value
                        assign v_match = true
                      elsif opt_index == 2 and variant.option2 == value
                        assign v_match = true
                      elsif opt_index == 3 and variant.option3 == value
                        assign v_match = true
                      endif
                      if v_match
                        if preview == 'buyable' or preview == 'low_stock'
                          assign v_any_available = true
                        elsif preview == 'sold_out'
                          assign v_any_available = v_any_available
                        elsif preview == 'first_sold_out'
                          unless forloop.first
                            assign v_any_available = true
                          endunless
                        elsif variant.available
                          assign v_any_available = true
                        endif
                        if section.settings.show_remaining and variant.inventory_management == 'shopify' and variant.inventory_quantity > 0 and variant.inventory_quantity <= section.settings.remaining_threshold
                          assign v_left = variant.inventory_quantity
                        endif
                        if preview == 'low_stock' and forloop.first
                          assign v_left = 12
                        endif
                      endif
                    endfor


                    comment
                      No launch date beside the options: the date or "Coming
                      soon" is said once, above the email field. Repeating it on
                      every row made the choice harder to read, not easier.
                    endcomment
                    assign v_note = ''
                    assign v_disabled = false
                    if product_state == 'available' and v_any_available == false
                      comment
                        Sold out, but still selectable: the visitor must be able
                        to choose the edition they actually want and leave an
                        email for it. Only a combination that does not exist at
                        all is unclickable.
                      endcomment
                      assign v_note = 'walterin.buy.sold_out' | t
                    elsif product_state == 'sold_out'
                      assign v_note = 'walterin.buy.sold_out' | t
                    elsif v_left > 0 and section.settings.remaining_text != blank
                      assign v_note = section.settings.remaining_text | replace: '[n]', v_left
                    endif

                    assign is_selected = false
                    if selected.options[forloop.index0] == value
                      assign is_selected = true
                    endif
                    if opt_index == 1 and selected.option1 == value
                      assign is_selected = true
                    elsif opt_index == 2 and selected.option2 == value
                      assign is_selected = true
                    elsif opt_index == 3 and selected.option3 == value
                      assign is_selected = true
                    endif
                  -%}
                  <label class="wui-choice">
                    <input
                      type="radio"
                      class="wui-choice__input"
                      name="wui-option-{{ opt_index }}-{{ section.id }}"
                      value="{{ value | escape }}"
                      data-wui-option="{{ opt_index }}"
                      data-wui-code="{{ v_code }}"
                      data-wui-name="{{ v_name | escape }}"
                      {% if is_selected %}
                        checked
                      {% endif %}
                      {% if v_disabled and is_selected == false %}
                        disabled
                      {% endif %}
                    >
                    <span class="wui-choice__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="wui-choice__text">
                      <span class="wui-choice__name">{{ v_name | escape | replace: '-', '&#8209;' }}</span>
                      <span class="wui-choice__note wui-small" data-wui-note {% if v_note == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ v_note | escape }}</span>
                    </span>
                  </label>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </fieldset>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
        {%- comment -%} The two helper lines sit with the choice they explain, not as their own group {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if wui.price_note != blank or wui.choice_note != blank -%}
          <div class="wui-buy__notes">
            {%- if wui.price_note != blank -%}
              <p class="wui-buy__note">{{ wui.price_note | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if wui.choice_note != blank -%}
              <p class="wui-buy__note wui-buy__note--second wui-small">{{ wui.choice_note | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <p class="wui-sr" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-wui-live></p>
        <p class="wui-status wui-buy__switched" data-wui-switched hidden></p>
        </div>
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- comment -%} ---- 4. Act ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The options are rendered once, above both calls to action, because a product
        can hold editions in different states at the same time: after 23 October the
        Prague eBook sells while the printed edition is still waiting for 10 November.
        Switching between them swaps the call to action without a page load, so both
        exist in the markup and JavaScript only hides and shows. Nothing is built on
        the fly, and with JavaScript off the visitor still sees the correct one for
        the edition the page was rendered with.

        The radios sit outside the cart form on purpose. They never carried the
        variant — the hidden id field does — so nothing is lost by moving them, and
        a form cannot be nested inside the notify form.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {{ option_groups }}

      {%- liquid
        assign selected_buyable = false
        if selected_launched and selected_available
          assign selected_buyable = true
        endif
      -%}

      {%- if product_state == 'sold_out' -%}
            <div class="wui-buy__cta">
              {%- assign sold_out_label = 'walterin.buy.sold_out' | t -%}
              {%- render 'wui-button', label: sold_out_label, block: true, attrs: 'disabled' -%}
            </div>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- if any_buyable -%}
          <div data-wui-cta-buy {% unless selected_buyable %}hidden{% endunless %}>
            <product-form class="wui-buy__form" data-section="{{ section.id }}">
              <div class="product-form__error-message-wrapper wui-status wui-status--error" role="alert" hidden>
                <span class="product-form__error-message"></span>
              </div>
              {%- form 'product', product, id: form_id, novalidate: 'novalidate', data-type: 'add-to-cart-form' -%}
                <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ selected.id }}" data-wui-variant-id>
                <div class="wui-buy__cta">
                  <button
                    type="submit"
                    name="add"
                    id="WuiSubmit-{{ section.id }}"
                    class="wui-btn wui-btn--block"
                    data-wui-submit
                    {% unless selected_available %}
                      disabled
                    {% endunless %}
                  >
                    <span data-wui-submit-label>
                      {%- if selected_available -%}
                        {{ section.settings.atc_label | escape }}
                        <span class="wui-num">· {{ price_html }}</span>
                      {%- else -%}
                        {{ 'walterin.buy.sold_out' | t }}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </span>
                    <span class="loading-overlay__spinner hidden wui-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  </button>
                  {%- if section.settings.show_express -%}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      What this button says is Shopify's decision, not ours: a wallet button when the
                      visitor's browser has Apple Pay, Google Pay or Shop Pay set up, and an unbranded
                      "Buy it now" when it does not. So the caption does the explaining — the same
                      words Shopify's own checkout uses above the same button.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <div class="wui-buy__express" data-wui-express {% if digital %}hidden{% endif %}>
                      {%- if section.settings.express_label != blank -%}
                        <span class="wui-buy__express-label">{{ section.settings.express_label | escape }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      {{ form | payment_button }}
                    </div>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- if section.settings.digital_note != blank -%}
                    <p class="wui-small wui-buy__digital" data-wui-digital {% unless digital %}hidden{% endunless %}>
                      {{- section.settings.digital_note | escape -}}
                    </p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- if section.settings.show_payment_icons and shop.enabled_payment_types.size > 0 -%}
                    <ul class="wui-pay" role="list" aria-label="{{ 'walterin.buy.payment_methods' | t | escape }}">
                      {%- assign hidden_types = section.settings.hide_payment_types | downcase | remove: ' ' | split: ',' -%}
                      {%- for type in shop.enabled_payment_types -%}
                        {%- assign type_key = type | downcase -%}
                        {%- unless hidden_types contains type_key -%}
                          <li>{{ type | payment_type_svg_tag: class: 'wui-pay__icon' }}</li>
                        {%- endunless -%}
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    </ul>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              {%- endform -%}
            </product-form>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if any_waiting -%}
          <div data-wui-cta-notify {% if selected_buyable %}hidden{% endif %}>
            <div class="wui-buy__cta" id="{{ notify_id }}-wrap">
              {%- form 'customer', id: notify_id, class: 'wui-notify', data-wui-notify: '' -%}
                {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
                  <p class="wui-status wui-status--success" role="status" tabindex="-1" data-wui-notify-done>
                    {%- liquid
                      assign notify_msg = section.settings.notify_success
                      if product.has_only_default_variant
                        assign notify_msg = notify_msg | replace: '[edition] ', '' | replace: '[edition]', ''
                      endif
                    -%}
                    {{ notify_msg | escape | replace: '[edition]', selected_name_html }}
                  </p>
                {%- else -%}
                  {%- assign tag_prefix = waitlist_tag -%}
                  {%- if request.design_mode and missing_sku -%}
                    <p class="wui-status">Theme editor only: this product's variants have no SKU, so
                      waitlist signups are tagged <code>{{ tag_prefix }}-v1</code>, <code>-v2</code> and so
                      on instead of by edition. Set a SKU on each variant in the product admin.</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <input
                    type="hidden"
                    name="contact[tags]"
                    value="{{ tag_prefix }}{% if selected_code != blank %},{{ tag_prefix }}-{{ selected_code }}{% endif %}"
                    data-wui-tag="{{ tag_prefix }},{{ tag_prefix }}-{ed}"
                  >
                  <input type="hidden" name="contact[accepts_marketing]" value="true">
                  <label class="wui-sr" for="{{ notify_id }}-email">{{ section.settings.notify_label | escape }}</label>
                  <div class="wui-notify__row">
                    <input
                      type="email"
                      id="{{ notify_id }}-email"
                      name="contact[email]"
                      class="wui-input"
                      placeholder="{{ section.settings.notify_placeholder | escape }}"
                      autocomplete="email"
                      required
                      data-wui-email
                      {% if form.errors %}
                        aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{ notify_id }}-error"
                      {% endif %}
                    >
                    {%- render 'wui-button', label: section.settings.notify_button, type: 'submit' -%}
                  </div>
                  {%- if form.errors -%}
                    <p class="wui-status wui-status--error" id="{{ notify_id }}-error" role="alert" data-wui-notify-error>
                      {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
                    </p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <label class="wui-check wui-small" for="{{ notify_id }}-newsletter">
                    <input type="checkbox" id="{{ notify_id }}-newsletter" class="wui-check__box" data-wui-newsletter>
                    <span>{{ 'walterin.notify.newsletter' | t }}</span>
                  </label>
                  <p class="wui-small wui-notify__note">
                    {{ 'walterin.notify.note' | t }}
                    <a class="wui-link" href="{{ shop.privacy_policy.url }}">{{ section.settings.privacy_link | escape }}</a>
                  </p>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endform -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} ---- 5. Read: accordions ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="wui-accordions">
        {%- comment -%}
          With nothing written in the section, the product's own description carries this accordion,
          so a brand-new product has a real page from the moment it is created.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign loc_prefix = 'walterin.product.' | append: product.handle | append: '_'
          assign about_lead = loc_prefix | append: 'about_lead' | t
          assign about_text = loc_prefix | append: 'about_text' | t
          assign has_locale = false
          unless about_lead contains 'Translation missing'
            assign has_locale = true
          endunless

          comment
            Each paragraph goes through wui-tail-nbsp so its last word is never left standing
            alone on a line — LINE-BREAKS.md, and the same treatment the cart options get.
          endcomment
          capture about_lead_t
            render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: about_lead
          endcapture
          capture about_text_t
            render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: about_text
          endcapture
          capture about_body
            if has_locale
              echo '<p>' | append: about_lead_t | append: '</p>'
              unless about_text contains 'Translation missing'
                echo '<p>' | append: about_text_t | append: '</p>'
              endunless
            else
              echo product.description
            endif
          endcapture
        -%}
        {%- assign about_heading = wui.about_heading | default: section.settings.about_heading -%}
        {%- if about_body != blank -%}
          <details class="wui-accordion" data-wui-acc>
            <summary>
              <span class="wui-accordion__title">
                <span class="wui-label">{{ about_heading | escape }}</span>
                {%- render 'wui-icon', icon: 'star', class: 'wui-accordion__star' -%}
              </span>
              <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="wui-accordion__wrap"><div class="wui-accordion__body wui-rte">{{ about_body }}</div></div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Only when there is something in it: a product with no box list and no specs would
          otherwise show an accordion with no heading and nothing inside.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          # Specs are one "Label: value" per line. Splitting on the FIRST colon only, so a value
          # that contains one ("Size: 129 × 207 mm") survives intact.
          assign spec_raw = wui.specs.value | default: ''
          assign spec_lines = spec_raw | strip | newline_to_br | replace: '<br>', '<br />' | split: '<br />'
          assign spec_count = 0
          for line in spec_lines
            assign l = line | strip
            if l != blank and l contains ':'
              assign spec_count = spec_count | plus: 1
            endif
          endfor

          assign box_has = false
          assign loc_box_probe = 'walterin.product.' | append: product.handle | append: '_box_lead' | t
          assign has_loc_box = false
          unless loc_box_probe contains 'Translation missing'
            assign has_loc_box = true
          endunless
          if wui.included != blank or spec_count > 0 or has_loc_box
            assign box_has = true
          endif
          if section.settings.box_heading == blank
            assign box_has = false
          endif
        -%}
        {%- if box_has -%}
        <details class="wui-accordion" data-wui-acc>
          <summary>
            <span class="wui-accordion__title">
              <span class="wui-label">{{ section.settings.box_heading | escape }}</span>
              {%- render 'wui-icon', icon: 'star', class: 'wui-accordion__star' -%}
            </span>
            <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="wui-accordion__wrap">
            <div class="wui-accordion__body">
              {%- comment -%}
                The first line of "What you get" is the summary and the bullets follow it. Both come
                from the one rich-text metafield, so the shape of the list is the merchant's choice.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                The box list from the language files when the product has one, otherwise the
                metafield. The nested bullet under "2 bonus cards" is why this is written out
                rather than split from rich text: a rich-text metafield cannot nest a list, and
                the second bonus card's description has to sit under it.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign box_lead = loc_prefix | append: 'box_lead' | t
                assign has_box = false
                unless box_lead contains 'Translation missing'
                  assign has_box = true
                endunless
                assign read_anchor = '#how-a-card-is-read'
              -%}
              {%- if has_box -%}
                <div class="wui-rte wui-included">
                  <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: box_lead -%}</p>
                  <ul>
                    <li>{%- assign v = loc_prefix | append: 'box_cards' | t -%}{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: v -%}</li>
                    <li>
                      {{ loc_prefix | append: 'box_bonus' | t }}
                      <ul>
                        <li>
                          {%- assign b1 = loc_prefix | append: 'box_bonus_1_html' | t -%}
                          {{ b1 | replace: '[READ_ANCHOR]', read_anchor }}
                        </li>
                        <li>{%- assign v = loc_prefix | append: 'box_bonus_2' | t -%}{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: v -%}</li>
                      </ul>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                  <p>{%- assign v = loc_prefix | append: 'box_box' | t -%}{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: v -%}</p>
                </div>
              {%- elsif wui.included != blank -%}
                <div class="wui-rte wui-included">{{ wui.included | metafield_tag }}</div>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if spec_count > 0 -%}
                <dl class="wui-dl">
                  {%- for line in spec_lines -%}
                    {%- assign l = line | strip -%}
                    {%- if l != blank and l contains ':' -%}
                      {%- assign label = l | split: ':' | first | strip -%}
                      {%- assign value = l | remove_first: label | remove_first: ':' | strip -%}
                      <dt>{{ label | escape }}</dt>
                      <dd>{{ value | escape }}</dd>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </dl>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                The GPSR row is OFF the product page (Veronka, 9 Oct 2026): it printed
                "Manufacturer: Walterin s. r. o., Ľubochnianska 4 … · support@walterin.com" and
                "Product: <title>" under every physical product.

                This is a legal question, not a tidy-up. Reg. (EU) 2023/988 Art. 19 asks for the
                manufacturer's name, postal and electronic address and a product identifier in the
                online offer, and taking them off the offer page leaves them only in the policies
                and the FAQ. It is written up as a question for the lawyer in
                docs/legal/LAWYER-QUESTIONS.md. Do not put it back, and do not delete the snippet,
                until that question is answered.
              {%- endcomment -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Delivery. The physical text stays hidden until Pack4you is signed (show_delivery_physical).
          The eBook text shows whenever a digital variant is selected.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.delivery_digital != blank or section.settings.show_delivery_physical -%}
          <details class="wui-accordion" data-wui-acc data-wui-delivery {% unless digital or section.settings.show_delivery_physical %}hidden{% endunless %}>
            <summary>
              <span class="wui-accordion__title">
                <span class="wui-label">{{ section.settings.delivery_heading | escape }}</span>
                {%- render 'wui-icon', icon: 'star', class: 'wui-accordion__star' -%}
              </span>
              <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="wui-accordion__wrap">
              <div class="wui-accordion__body">
                {%- if section.settings.delivery_digital != blank -%}
                  <div class="wui-rte" data-wui-delivery-digital {% unless digital %}hidden{% endunless %}>
                    {{ section.settings.delivery_digital }}
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if section.settings.show_delivery_physical and section.settings.delivery_physical != blank -%}
                  <div class="wui-rte" data-wui-delivery-physical {% if digital %}hidden{% endif %}>
                    {{ section.settings.delivery_physical }}
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The legal guarantee is NOT on the product page (Veronka, 7 October 2026).

          It lives in one place in the shop now — "Legal guarantee" in the footer's OFFICIAL
          column, which opens the official EU notice in colour on the first click — plus Terms
          clause 10. Not here, not in the header, not on Shop, not in the cart or checkout, and
          not in the order email.

          Before re-adding it here, read docs/legal/legal-guarantee-placement-research.md: this
          was a decision taken against a written recommendation, with the reasoning on both sides
          recorded. It is not an oversight and not a leftover.
        {%- endcomment -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The extra accordions, from the product's own metafields. One rich-text field holds them
          all: every Heading 3 starts a new accordion and everything under it is that accordion's
          text. They are all secondary — a dashed rule and no star — because they sit under About,
          What you get and Delivery, which are the ones that answer "what is this thing".

          The before-launch accordion is appended only while the product cannot be bought, so it
          takes itself off the page on launch day with nobody having to remember it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          metafield_tag wraps each field in <div class="metafield-rich_text_field">…</div>. Split on
          '<h3' throws the opening tag away with the first chunk, but the closing one rides along
          inside the last accordion's body — one unmatched </div> that closed the buy column early
          and left the variants <script> outside its own root, killing the whole variant engine.
          So take the wrapper off each field before the split, not after. The rendered rich text
          itself is untouched: only metafield_tag's own container goes.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The "When can I have it?" accordion is gone (Veronka, 9 Oct 2026). It came from
          wui.preorder_note while a product could not be bought; nothing replaces it. The launch
          pill in the price row already says "Coming soon" or the date, and the notify form below
          it already asks for the email, so this said a third time what the page says twice.
          The metafield is left alone in admin — nothing reads it now.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          capture notes_html
            if wui.notes != blank
              capture notes_raw
                echo wui.notes | metafield_tag
              endcapture
              echo notes_raw | remove_first: '<div class="metafield-rich_text_field">' | remove_last: '</div>'
            endif
          endcapture
          assign note_chunks = notes_html | split: '<h3'
        -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Words from the theme's language files for the products that have them, and from the
          product's own metafields for the ones that do not.

          This is a deliberate departure from docs/CONTENT-MODEL.md, which says a product's words
          live in metafields because "metafields survive a theme change". That reason is real and
          it is why the fallback below stays. It is outweighed here by the one failure this site
          keeps repeating: a metafield's Slovak lives in Translate & Adapt, outside the repo, and
          has gone unwritten every single time — the home page, the FAQ and these accordions were
          all English on /sk/. In the locale files the two languages sit together, are reviewed in
          a diff, publish with the theme, and can be previewed before they go live, which a
          metafield cannot.

          Veronka: if you would rather these lived in metafields, say so and I will move them —
          it is the same text either way, and the fallback path below already does the work.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if has_locale -%}
          {%- render 'wui-product-notes', product: product, prefix: loc_prefix -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The metafield path runs only for a product with no locale entry. Running both would
          print "As a gift" twice on the tarot, whose metafield still holds the old wording.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- unless has_locale -%}
        {%- for chunk in note_chunks -%}
          {%- if chunk contains '</h3>' -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign head_raw = chunk | split: '</h3>' | first
              assign note_heading = head_raw | split: '>' | last | strip
              assign note_body = chunk | split: '</h3>' | last
            -%}
            {%- if note_heading != blank -%}
              <details class="wui-accordion wui-accordion--suggest" data-wui-acc>
                <summary>
                  <span class="wui-accordion__title">
                    <span class="wui-label">{{ note_heading | escape }}</span>
                  </span>
                  <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </summary>
                <div class="wui-accordion__wrap"><div class="wui-accordion__body wui-rte">{{ note_body }}</div></div>
              </details>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} ================= Mobile sticky bar ================= {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.show_sticky -%}
    <div class="wui-sticky" data-wui-sticky inert>
      {%- if product.featured_media -%}
        <span class="wui-sticky__thumb">
          {{- product.featured_media | image_url: width: 120 | image_tag: alt: '', loading: 'lazy', width: 40, height: 40 -}}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <p class="wui-sticky__text">
        <span class="wui-label">{{ wui.short_title | default: product.title | escape }}</span>
        <span class="wui-small">{{ price_html }} · {{ selected_name_html }}</span>
      </p>
      {%- comment -%}
        The bar mirrors the column above it, for the same reason: an edition can
        be on sale while the one next to it is still waiting for its date, so
        both controls exist and JavaScript shows the right one. Without
        JavaScript the visitor keeps whichever the page was rendered with.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if product_state != 'sold_out' -%}
        {%- if any_buyable -%}
          <button
            type="submit"
            name="add"
            form="{{ form_id }}"
            class="wui-btn wui-btn--sm"
            data-wui-sticky-submit
            data-wui-cta-buy
            {% unless selected_buyable %}
              hidden
            {% endunless %}
            {% unless selected_available %}
              disabled
            {% endunless %}
          >
            {{- section.settings.atc_label | escape -}}
          </button>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if any_waiting -%}
          {%- capture notify_href -%}#{{ notify_id }}-wrap{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- capture notify_attrs -%}
            data-wui-focus-notify data-wui-cta-notify {% if selected_buyable %}hidden{% endif %}
          {%- endcapture -%}
          {%- render 'wui-button',
            label: section.settings.notify_button,
            href: notify_href,
            size: 'sm',
            attrs: notify_attrs
          -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} Variant data for walterin-buy.js (availability matrix, prices, shipping) {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="application/json" data-wui-variants>
    [
      {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
        {%- liquid
          capture j_launch
            render 'launch-date', product: product, variant: variant
          endcapture
          assign j_launch = j_launch | strip
          assign j_launched = true
          if j_launch == 'soon'
            assign j_launched = false
          elsif j_launch != blank
            assign j_launch_n = j_launch | plus: 0
            if j_launch_n > today
              assign j_launched = false
            endif
          endif
          if preview == 'buyable' or preview == 'first_sold_out' or preview == 'low_stock'
            assign j_launched = true
          endif
          assign j_label = ''
          if j_launched == false
            if j_launch == 'soon'
              assign j_label = 'walterin.launch.soon' | t
            else
              assign j_key = 'walterin.launch.date_' | append: j_launch
              assign j_name = j_key | t
              assign j_label = 'walterin.launch.from' | t | replace: '[date]', j_name
            endif
          endif
        -%}
        {
          "id": {{ variant.id }},
          "options": {{ variant.options | json }},
          "available": {% if preview == 'buyable' or preview == 'low_stock' %}true{% elsif preview == 'first_sold_out' %}{% if forloop.first %}false{% else %}true{% endif %}{% elsif preview == 'sold_out' %}false{% else %}{{ variant.available }}{% endif %},
          {%- comment -%}
            launched: has this edition's date passed? date: the line to show
            while it has not. Both come from snippets/launch-date.liquid, so the
            page and the script can never disagree about when something opens.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          "launched": {{ j_launched }},
          "date": {{ j_label | json }},
          "price": {{ variant.price | money_without_trailing_zeros | json }},
          "shipping": {{ variant.requires_shipping }},
          "left": {% if section.settings.show_remaining and variant.inventory_management == 'shopify' and variant.inventory_quantity > 0 and variant.inventory_quantity <= section.settings.remaining_threshold %}{{ variant.inventory_quantity }}{% elsif preview == 'low_stock' and forloop.first %}12{% else %}0{% endif %}
        }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  </script>
  {%- if section.settings.remaining_text != blank -%}
    <span hidden data-wui-remaining-template>{{ section.settings.remaining_text | escape }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- liquid
  if selected.featured_media
    assign seo_media = selected.featured_media
  else
    assign seo_media = product.featured_media
  endif
-%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "http://schema.org/",
    "@type": "Product",
    "name": {{ product.title | json }},
    "url": {{ request.origin | append: product.url | json }},
    {% if seo_media -%}
      "image": [{{ seo_media | image_url: width: 1920 | prepend: "https:" | json }}],
    {%- endif %}
    "description": {{ product.description | strip_html | json }},
    "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": {{ product.vendor | json }} },
    "offers": [
      {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
        {
          "@type": "Offer",
          {%- if variant.sku != blank -%}"sku": {{ variant.sku | json }},{%- endif -%}
          "availability": "http://schema.org/{% if variant.available %}InStock{% else %}OutOfStock{% endif %}",
          "price": {{ variant.price | divided_by: 100.00 | json }},
          "priceCurrency": {{ cart.currency.iso_code | json }},
          "url": {{ request.origin | append: variant.url | json }}
        }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  }
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Section rhythm: 48 above (24 on phones), 96 below (48 on phones) */

  .wui .wui-buy__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--wui-24); }
  .wui .wui-buy__grid > * { min-width: 0; }
  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    .wui .wui-buy__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--wui-48); align-items: start; }
  }

  /* Gallery: scroll-snap strip (swipes on touch, works without JS: thumbs are anchors) */
  @media (min-width: 990px) { .wui .wui-buy__gallery { position: sticky; top: var(--wui-24); } }
  .wui .wui-gallery__main { position: relative; aspect-ratio: 1; }
  .wui .wui-gallery__track {
    display: flex;
    height: 100%;
    overflow-x: auto;
    overflow-y: hidden;
    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
    scrollbar-width: none;
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
  }
  .wui .wui-gallery__track::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
  .wui .wui-gallery__slide { flex: 0 0 100%; height: 100%; scroll-snap-align: start; }
  .wui .wui-gallery__zoom { display: block; height: 100%; cursor: zoom-in; }
  .wui .wui-gallery__slide img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .wui .wui-gallery__count {
    position: absolute;
    right: var(--wui-12);
    bottom: var(--wui-12);
    padding: 4px var(--wui-8);
    font-family: var(--wui-body);
    font-size: var(--wui-fs-small);
    line-height: 1.2;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    background: var(--wui-paper);
    border: var(--wui-line) solid var(--wui-ink);
    border-radius: var(--wui-radius);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  /* Phones: the swipe strip and the counter are the navigation; thumbs would push the title down */
  .wui .wui-gallery__thumbs { display: none; }
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .wui .wui-gallery__thumbs {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(80px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--wui-12);
      margin-top: var(--wui-12);
      padding: 0 var(--wui-sh) var(--wui-sh) 0; /* room for the selected thumb's shadow */
    }
  }
  .wui .wui-gallery__thumb {
    display: block;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: var(--wui-line) solid var(--wui-ink);
    border-radius: var(--wui-radius);
    background: var(--wui-paper);
    transition: box-shadow var(--wui-t-hover) var(--wui-ease);
  }
  .wui .wui-gallery__thumb img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .wui .wui-gallery__thumb:hover { box-shadow: var(--wui-shadow-hover); }
  .wui .wui-gallery__thumb[aria-current='true'] { box-shadow: var(--wui-shadow); outline: 3px solid var(--wui-yellow); outline-offset: -5.5px; }

  /* Buy column: title → price → choices → button → accordions, one group apart (40 / 32) */
  /* Groups, top to bottom: what it is (title + price) · what you choose (legend, pills, the two
     helper lines) · what you do (button, wallets, icons) · what you can read (accordions).
     Inside a group nothing is further apart than 16; between groups 32 (24 on phones); the
     accordions are a different job, so they get 48 (32). */
  .wui .wui-buy__box { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--wui-24); }
  @media (min-width: 750px) { .wui .wui-buy__box { gap: var(--wui-32, 32px); } }
  .wui .wui-buy__head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .wui .wui-buy__title { line-height: 1.05; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .wui .wui-buy__price { display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--wui-8) var(--wui-16); margin-top: var(--wui-16); }
  @media (min-width: 750px) { .wui .wui-buy__price { margin-top: var(--wui-24); } }
  .wui .wui-buy__amount { font-family: var(--wui-body); font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--wui-fs-price); line-height: 1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .wui .wui-buy__ship { font-size: var(--wui-fs-body); line-height: 1.45; }
  .wui .wui-buy__option + .wui-buy__option { margin-top: var(--wui-24); }
  /* flex, so the legend is a normal item: a floated legend in a block fieldset shrinks the
     grid next to it to zero width */
  .wui .wui-buy__fieldset { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--wui-16); border: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0; min-width: 0; }
  .wui .wui-buy__legend { float: left; width: 100%; padding: 0; }
  .wui .wui-buy__choices { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .wui .wui-buy__notes { margin-top: var(--wui-12); } /* control → helper */
  .wui .wui-buy__note { font-size: var(--wui-fs-body); line-height: 1.45; }
  .wui .wui-buy__note--second { margin-top: var(--wui-8); font-size: var(--wui-fs-small); line-height: 1.45; } /* helper ↔ helper, supporting */
  .wui .wui-buy__switched { margin-top: var(--wui-12); }
  .wui .wui-buy__box > .wui-accordions { margin-top: var(--wui-8); } /* 24 + 8 = 32 on phones */
  @media (min-width: 750px) { .wui .wui-buy__box > .wui-accordions { margin-top: var(--wui-16); } } /* 32 + 16 = 48 */
  .wui .wui-buy__form form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--wui-group); }
  .wui .wui-buy__cta { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--wui-12); }
  /* Inset lives on .shopify-payment-button alone (assets/walterin-ui.css): applying it here as
     well double-inset the wallet button, leaving its ink ring 3px right of Add to cart. */
  .wui .wui-notify { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .wui .wui-notify__row { display: flex; gap: var(--wui-12); }
  .wui .wui-notify__row .wui-input { flex: 1; }
  .wui .wui-notify__row .wui-btn { flex: none; }
  .wui .wui-check { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--wui-8); margin-top: var(--wui-16); cursor: pointer; }
  .wui .wui-check__box { flex: none; width: 20px; height: 20px; margin: 0; accent-color: var(--wui-ink, #222); }
  .wui .wui-notify__note { margin-top: var(--wui-8); }
  @media (max-width: 479px) {
    .wui .wui-notify__row { flex-direction: column; }
    .wui .wui-notify__row .wui-btn { width: calc(100% - var(--wui-sh)); }
  }
  /* Everything with a hard shadow keeps the shadow inside the column edge */
  .wui .wui-buy__cta .wui-btn--block { width: calc(100% - var(--wui-sh)); }
  .wui .wui-buy__cta .wui-btn { margin-right: var(--wui-sh); margin-bottom: var(--wui-sh); }
  .wui .wui-buy__cta .wui-btn--block { margin-right: var(--wui-sh); }

  /* Payment icons: only the methods the shop really has */
  .wui .wui-pay { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; justify-content: center; }
  .wui .wui-pay__icon { display: block; width: 38px; height: 24px; }

  /* Mobile sticky bar: content aligns with the page edges */
  .wui .wui-sticky { display: none; }
  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .wui .wui-sticky {
      position: fixed;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      z-index: 20;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      /* wraps rather than truncating the call to action when text scaling is turned up */
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      row-gap: var(--wui-8);
      gap: var(--wui-12);
      padding: var(--wui-12) var(--wui-edge) calc(var(--wui-12) + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
      background: var(--wui-paper);
      border-top: var(--wui-line) solid var(--wui-ink);
      transform: translateY(110%);
      transition: transform 0.25s var(--wui-ease);
    }
    .wui .wui-sticky.is-shown { transform: none; }
  }
  .wui .wui-sticky__thumb { flex: none; width: 40px; height: 40px; overflow: hidden; border: var(--wui-line) solid var(--wui-ink); border-radius: 6px; }
  .wui .wui-sticky__thumb img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .wui .wui-sticky__text { flex: 1 1 8em; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
  .wui .wui-sticky__text .wui-label { font-size: var(--wui-fs-body); }
  /* flex:none + nowrap meant the button could not give way: with Android text scaling on, its
     label grew and pushed the whole bar past the right edge of the screen. It may now shrink, and
     the label truncates rather than dragging the page sideways. */
  .wui .wui-sticky .wui-btn {
    flex: 0 0 auto; min-width: 0; max-width: 100%;
    white-space: nowrap; margin-right: 3px;
  }
  .wui .wui-sticky__text .wui-label,
  .wui .wui-sticky__text .wui-small { overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }

  /* Price and availability cross-fade instead of swapping (walterin-buy.js) */
  .wui [data-wui-price],
  .wui [data-wui-edname],
  .wui [data-wui-note] { transition: opacity 90ms var(--wui-ease); }
  .wui .is-fading { opacity: 0; }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Walterin · Buy",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "wui-section",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": [
      "product"
    ]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "editor_state",
      "label": "Preview state (theme editor only)",
      "info": "Review the other states here. Visitors always see the real product state.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "real",
          "label": "Real product state"
        },
        {
          "value": "buyable",
          "label": "Launch day: everything buyable"
        },
        {
          "value": "low_stock",
          "label": "Launch day: low stock"
        },
        {
          "value": "first_sold_out",
          "label": "Launch day: first option sold out"
        },
        {
          "value": "sold_out",
          "label": "Sold out"
        }
      ],
      "default": "real"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Gallery"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Uses the product's images. Set alt text and focal points in the product admin. Tapping an image opens full-screen zoom (pinch, double-tap, swipe)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "gallery_label",
      "label": "Gallery label (screen readers)",
      "default": "Product images. Swipe or use the arrow keys."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "thumbs_label",
      "label": "Thumbnail label (screen readers)",
      "default": "Image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "zoom_label",
      "label": "Enlarge label (screen readers)",
      "default": "Enlarge image"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Choices"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "One group per product option, added automatically. The name of each value follows the site language via Translate & Adapt, and the waitlist tag uses the variant SKU."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_remaining",
      "label": "Show copies left when stock is low",
      "info": "Needs inventory tracking on the variants. Switch on at launch.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "remaining_threshold",
